_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"f7e973b1fee8997f88517421fe8f0966056f31da7be51791cc109113e63bbe72","event_uuid":"fc1c6a3b-a91d-4485-9eb6-76e80f2728b3","position":{"commit_sha":"16cec7cec682b1e897c968f06545076f824d91a5","position":"1795063706370705708-fc1c6a3b-a91d-4485-9eb6-76e80f2728b3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root cause confirmed (AC1) test by test from Windows job 133527199439 (run 43932173744): e.g. `assert 'tests\\\\test_thing.py' == 'tests/test_thing.py'` (check_destructive_test_exec), `src\\\\rebar\\\\live.py:1: deprecated vocabulary` (criteria vocabulary), `ValueError: path is on mount 'C:', start on mount 'D:'` (check_skill_frontmatter relpath), `'infra\\\\scripts\\\\foo.sh' == 'infra/scripts/foo.sh'` (deploy manifest), `OSError: [WinError 10106]` at `import asyncio` in children whose hand-built env lacks SYSTEMROOT (llm_framework, tracing, fs_tools, fixture_heal), `.endswith(\"/.rebar/scratch\")` / `str(relative_to)` test asserts, and a missing `pypandoc/files/pandoc` on an unpinned platform. The 21 shell-stub lines are the posix-shell root cause and moved to citreous-talented-wildebeest.\n\nRegressions (AC2), run on the pre-fix scripts: 4 failed for the expected reason (`'src\\\\rebar\\\\live.py:1: ...'.startswith('src/rebar/live.py:1: ')` False; `FAIL: ../../../../...` instead of absolute POSIX path; `['tests\\\\test_thing.py'] != ['tests/test_thing.py']`; `_repo_relative` missing). `test_subprocess_env_minimal.py` errored at import (no `minimal_env`). After the fix all pass; 307 tests across the touched modules pass on macOS. Commit d287c64641a (stacked on d782dd17ea6) deletes path-separators.args and posix-shell.args and their test.yml references.","timestamp":1795028644360779572},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed as Gerrit 3429 (`a97925e9d3b`), stacked on 3428. It deletes path-separators.args and posix-shell.args. `make verify` passed at the stack top (3430): exit 0.","timestamp":1795037734391273058}],"created_at":1794857639509705422,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f53c482f-66ae-4e32-b5fa-b508bb0cd7dd","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"6798-606d-37dc-46e7"},{"link_uuid":"2dd56232-de85-4555-8a34-a2774fe72e27","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"02ae-c4ba-a9ce-4e38"},{"link_uuid":"fc1c6a3b-a91d-4485-9eb6-76e80f2728b3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ea2d-ac49-6b46-4580"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from majestic-depilatory-beetle. The advisory `sweep (windows)` job deselects the 42 tests in `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/path-separators.args` (runs at `b4e0d01b649`, 2026-11-15/16).\n\nRoot causes, confirmed test by test from Windows job 133527199439 (run 43932173744):\n\n1. **Repo scripts emit native separators (product, 14 tests).** Repo-relative paths are formatted with `str(path)`, so Windows prints `src\\rebar\\live.py` where the contract (and CI annotations) is `src/rebar/live.py`: `scripts/check_destructive_test_exec.py:126`, `scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py` (findings built from `relative_to`, e.g. `:289`), `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py:213`, `scripts/check_uv_pin.py:228,249,260,576,592`. `scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py` calls `os.path.relpath(path, REPO_ROOT)` at `:129` (`_emit_github`) and `:162` (`main`), which raises `ValueError: path is on mount 'C:', start on mount 'D:'` for a file on another drive and prints `..`/backslash paths otherwise.\n2. **The same defect in `scripts/check_deploy_manifest.py:99,160`** (`str(p.relative_to(repo_root))`), whose 7 tests in `tests/unit/test_check_deploy_manifest.py` were filed under `posix-shell.args`; this ticket fixes and un-deselects them.\n3. **Hand-built subprocess environments drop `SYSTEMROOT` (4 tests).** `tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py:35`, `tests/unit/test_tracing.py:97`, `tests/unit/test_fs_tools_extraction.py:61` and `tests/unit/test_fixture_heal.py:320` pass a from-scratch `env`; without `SYSTEMROOT` Windows cannot load Winsock, so `import asyncio` fails with `OSError: [WinError 10106]`.\n4. **Test-only separator asserts (2 tests).** `tests/unit/test_config_ev3a_aliases.py:100,108` assert `.endswith(\"/.rebar/scratch\")`; `tests/unit/test_repo_snapshot.py:344,388,505` compare `str(p.relative_to(root))` with git's POSIX names.\n5. **No pinned Pandoc for the platform (1 test).** `tests/unit/reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py:417` validates the installed Pandoc against `SUPPORTED_PANDOC_BINARY_SHA256` (`scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py:56`, `darwin-arm64` and `linux-x86_64` only); `windows-x86_64` has no pinned binary to match.\n\nThe remaining 21 lines are shell or shebang command stubs, owned and un-deselected by bug citreous-talented-wildebeest.\n\n## Approach\n\n- (1, 2) Format each emitted repo-relative path with `PurePath.as_posix()`. In `check_skill_frontmatter.py`, add one `_display_path(path: Path) -> str` helper (`path.resolve().relative_to(REPO_ROOT).as_posix()`, falling back to `path.resolve().as_posix()` on `ValueError` for a file outside the repo) and use it at both `:129` and `:162` instead of `os.path.relpath`. One spelling of a path across hosts is what the scripts' consumers (tests, CI annotations, baselines) already assume.\n- (3) Add `minimal_env(**values) -> SubprocessEnv` to `tests/_subprocess_env.py` (existing helper module, no new mechanism) that copies `SYSTEMROOT` from `os.environ` when present and adds the given values; the four tests build their env with it.\n- (4) Compare against `str(Path(...))` / `.as_posix()`.\n- (5) Skip that one test when `current_platform_key()` has no pinned fingerprint, with that reason; on the two pinned platforms it still runs.\n- Remove the 21 fixed lines from `path-separators.args` and the 7 manifest lines from `posix-shell.args`; whichever of this change and citreous-talented-wildebeest lands second deletes the emptied argfile(s) and their `@` lines in `.github/workflows/test.yml`.\n\nPortability: `as_posix()` and `relative_to` are pure-path operations; `SYSTEMROOT` is only copied when the host defines it.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `scripts/check_destructive_test_exec.py`, `scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py`, `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`, `scripts/check_uv_pin.py`, `scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py`, `scripts/check_deploy_manifest.py`\n- `tests/_subprocess_env.py`, `tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py`, `tests/unit/test_tracing.py`, `tests/unit/test_fs_tools_extraction.py`, `tests/unit/test_fixture_heal.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_config_ev3a_aliases.py`, `tests/unit/test_repo_snapshot.py`, `tests/unit/reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py`\n- Regression tests added to `tests/scripts/test_check_destructive_test_exec.py`, `tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py`, `tests/unit/test_check_skill_frontmatter.py`, `tests/unit/test_check_deploy_manifest.py`, and a new `tests/unit/test_subprocess_env_minimal.py`\n- `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/path-separators.args`, `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-shell.args`, `.github/workflows/test.yml`\n\n## Testing\n\n- Linux-gate regressions that fail before the fix: pass a `PureWindowsPath` relative path through each script's formatting seam (`scan_file`'s `rel`, the deploy-manifest resolver, the vocabulary finding) and assert the emitted string uses `/`. For `check_skill_frontmatter`, run `main` on a bad `SKILL.md` under `tmp_path` with `capsys` and assert the line starts with `FAIL: {p.resolve().as_posix()}:` (pre-fix, `relpath` prints a `../..` path, so it fails), and assert `_emit_github` names the same path in `file=`. `minimal_env` carries `SYSTEMROOT` when it is set and omits it when unset.\n- The 28 listed tests pass under `make verify`.\n- Windows: `gh workflow run test.yml --ref main` after merge.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The class's root cause is recorded on this ticket with the evidence that confirmed it.\n- [ ] Each new regression test fails against the pre-fix script or helper and passes after (outcomes recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] Every line removed from `path-separators.args` names a test that passed, or skipped with a capability reason, in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `sweep (windows)` concludes `success` on that run.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/check_destructive_test_exec.py","reason":"emit POSIX separators"},{"path":"scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py","reason":"emit POSIX separators"},{"path":"scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py","reason":"emit POSIX separators"},{"path":"scripts/check_uv_pin.py","reason":"emit POSIX separators"},{"path":"scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py","reason":"cross-drive safe display path"},{"path":"scripts/check_deploy_manifest.py","reason":"emit POSIX separators"},{"path":"tests/_subprocess_env.py","reason":"minimal_env keeps SYSTEMROOT"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py","reason":"use minimal_env"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_tracing.py","reason":"use minimal_env"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_fs_tools_extraction.py","reason":"use minimal_env"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_fixture_heal.py","reason":"use minimal_env"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_config_ev3a_aliases.py","reason":"platform path compare"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_repo_snapshot.py","reason":"as_posix compare"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py","reason":"skip when no pinned pandoc for platform"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_check_destructive_test_exec.py","reason":"regression test"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py","reason":"regression test"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_check_skill_frontmatter.py","reason":"regression test"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_check_deploy_manifest.py","reason":"regression test"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_subprocess_env_minimal.py","reason":"new minimal_env tests"},{"path":".github/windows-sweep-deselect/path-separators.args","reason":"remove fixed lines"},{"path":".github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-shell.args","reason":"remove 7 manifest lines"},{"path":".github/workflows/test.yml","reason":"drop @ reference when argfile deleted"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","02ae-c4ba-a9ce-4e38"],["relates_to","ea2d-ac49-6b46-4580"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"7db86de0-93d4-4f9a-b42b-94de747dba86","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"453c-cad2-fab5-456d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: emitted and asserted paths use the native separator (42 tests)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["879e11f7-65b3-4f1e-946a-679db5df8b76","9dcea388-5986-4468-9510-3184bc5e3733","fba8ffe7-730d-48c4-863c-78098692eda7","1903b79a-f81e-4c02-a02d-e496de4e614f","b20738de-cd2f-4ba1-b97d-b7a9397dc80a","7db86de0-93d4-4f9a-b42b-94de747dba86","75c0b254-798e-470b-aa9d-c5c526500c4f","01a6bf59-af36-45bc-824a-19255bd326cc","24311db7-b66b-48b9-af60-3fdc6db36d84","2dd56232-de85-4555-8a34-a2774fe72e27","fc1c6a3b-a91d-4485-9eb6-76e80f2728b3"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f